00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:41.220
So quick story actually, I
came to SF like two days ago.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.920
I flew down from Seattle.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.452
So I'm in the airplane in
the aisle doing my work.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.285
So I have my laptop.

00:04:47.285 --> 00:04:49.634
It has all my
developer tools on it.

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:51.300
I've been using it
for a year and a half

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:54.170
so I have all my languages,
all my GCP tools.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:56.360
I'm doing my work and
then out of nowhere--

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.960
and this is a true story, by
the way-- on my left hand,

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.970
I start noticing some Coke
appearing then on my hand

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:05.510
and then on my laptop and,
like, all over my laptop.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:08.240
And I look up and the actual
flight attendant by mistake

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.970
just dropped everything
on my laptop.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.950
I always wondered if
that actually happened.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.730
But it actually
does, so heads up.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.110
This might happen to you.

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:17.190
So I get back to SF.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.370
I'm like, great.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.370
Obviously my data's all
backed up, but I'm like,

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.400
I have to get a new machine
and reinstall everything.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.640
And for me to be even
productive minimally,

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:27.040
I have to do all of that.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:30.270
And my first thought was, if
only I could log on somewhere

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.960
and have everything preinstall
and I can just hook up my data

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.130
and I'll be up and running.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:36.640
Anyways, kind of
wishful thinking.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.750
But then I realized, this is
exactly what Cloud Shell does.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.900
So in reality, Cloud
Shell, no kidding,

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.940
is a command line interface
where you log on in the Cloud

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.580
and you literally get access
to a bunch of GCP tools

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.590
and you can start being
productive right away.

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:52.210
So by the way, this
was not a set up story.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.950
This actually happened and
it just clicked in my mind,

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:54.720
this is amazing.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.702
This is perfect timing for this.

00:05:58.702 --> 00:06:00.160
So literally, what
actually happens

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.050
is you only need a browser.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:04.960
You log on, nothing
to install locally,

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.340
and right there, you have a
bunch of tools pre-installed.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.820
And by tools, they
mean like text editors,

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.550
we have Emacs,
VIM, you have Nano.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.540
You have Git preinstalled,
the Cloud SDK,

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.000
which is a bunch of CLIs.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.289
And Aylin will talk about
that a little bit later.

00:06:18.289 --> 00:06:20.080
But everything is
pre-installed up to date,

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.580
you have nothing to do.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.020
And we support seven
languages out of the box.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:28.510
So we have Java, Go, Dot
Net, Node, PHP, Python, Ruby,

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:30.910
the interpreters, the
compilers, the package managers,

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:34.200
you can do pip install,
it's all there.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.980
And the beauty is that it
has built in authorization

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.510
so no need to log on again.

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:41.380
You can just execute
and it just works.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.340
I could give you guys
more and more features,

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.423
but it would probably be
easier if I just show you

00:06:45.423 --> 00:06:46.840
how it works in the console.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.080
So we'll switch to demo.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:50.220
Lovely.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.900
So what we're
looking at right now

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.770
is literally the main landing
page when you log onto GCB.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.260
If you've done this before,
this is not new to you.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.540
You're looking at projects
and every Cloud resource

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:04.200
you create will be
within a project.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.860
So to manage these resources,
if you go to the top left corner

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.640
and you click on that,
you'll see a menu

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:10.200
with basically a bunch of--

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:15.719
so if you click on that,
you will see a menu

00:07:15.719 --> 00:07:17.510
with a bunch of the
services, some of which

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:18.850
we talked about earlier.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.851
App Engine and Compute
Engine, Container Engine.

00:07:20.851 --> 00:07:22.350
Anyways, the point
being is that you

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:24.620
can use that to do your
management through the UI.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.870
But like we talked, what if you
want to run some automation,

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:28.190
you want to write
some code, you want

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.410
to-- well you'll probably
need a shell for that.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.390
So if you go to the
top right corner,

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.820
you'll notice there's
an Activate Cloud Shell.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:37.314
You click on that and that
will start the Cloud Shell.

00:07:37.314 --> 00:07:38.730
So what happens
in the background,

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:41.271
just to let you know, is that
a virtual machine, a small one,

00:07:41.271 --> 00:07:44.290
gets created and it has
all the tools pre-installed

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.430
right there.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.550
And what it does is it mounts
five gigabytes of storage

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:49.250
that you own.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:50.860
So every person
here, when you log on

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.560
with your Google account, you
get 5 gig of persisted disk

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:54.666
storage for free.

00:07:54.666 --> 00:07:57.040
And that gets mounted as your
home directory in the Cloud

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.380
Shell because it's
mounted on the VM.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:01.120
So if you do a PWD,
for example, you

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.664
will see that we're in the
home directory of where we are.

00:08:03.664 --> 00:08:05.830
And everything you save in
there will get persisted.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.840
So if you log off, you
come back in a week,

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:08.990
everything you
save will be there.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:11.364
So you can see how you can
start writing scripts, writing

00:08:11.364 --> 00:08:14.200
automation, writing some code,
everything will be saved.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.260
And also just to show you if
we do get dash dash version,

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:20.360
you'll see that we have
that installed as well.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.609
Now, we talked about
VIM, talk about Emacs.

00:08:22.609 --> 00:08:25.150
There's always a big war between
the two, which one's better.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:27.730
We have a solution
[INAUDIBLE] which

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:31.210
is basically to go in
the top left corner,

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.580
you'll see here files.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:37.250
And if you click on
launching the code editor,

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:39.440
this is experimental right
now but this is basically

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:42.890
a UI for you to be able to do
coding directly in the browser.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:45.341
So if you're more into that
and using a user interface,

00:08:45.341 --> 00:08:46.340
this is what you can do.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:48.089
And notice here that
what we're looking at

00:08:48.089 --> 00:08:49.640
is your home directory
also mounted.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:50.870
So whatever you save
in there will get

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:52.550
persisted again
just like earlier.

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.530
It's the same view.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.840
So we talked about
having the tools,

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.700
we talked about
having a code editor.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:08:59.800
Everything is pre-set up.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.650
We have five gigabytes of space.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:04.400
So in the next part, we'll just
really create a very small web

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.670
app in Python just to show
you what can actually be done.

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:09.590
And it will walk through
some of the workflows

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:12.020
so you can get a better idea
of what's enabled directly

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:15.101
from the console again without
installing anything locally.

00:09:15.101 --> 00:09:16.350
So let's go ahead and do that.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:19.700
So we'll create a new
app we'll call it My App.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.580
And that will be a Python web
app, so exactly very simple.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:26.160
So first thing we'll do,
we'll create a main.py,

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.890
and that will contain
our main code.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:31.110
Now we could go ahead
and do that but if you're

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:32.791
familiar with App
Engine Standard,

00:09:32.791 --> 00:09:35.040
we do have a quick start in
there that explains to you

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:37.050
exactly how to get started and
this is exactly where we're

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.440
going to go and copy that code.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.050
Again, the goal is to
make it very simple

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:42.550
just to show you the other
tools that we have around that.

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:45.420
So in this case, you see that
we have a very simple web

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.110
application.

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.300
We'll copy that in.

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.400
And what it does
is imports webapp2

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.470
which is a app engine
standard web framework.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:55.406
Then we register a get handler
where we just print out

00:09:55.406 --> 00:09:57.030
Hello World, where
we could change that

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.100
to Hello Next for instance.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.170
And then we're going
to register the app--

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:02.930
for the handler, I mean.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:04.100
So that is done, we're done.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.560
That is the simplest possible
web app we can do in Python.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:10.167
But given that we want to run
